1. **A focus detection device comprising:**

a two-dimensional micro-lens array including a plurality of micro-lenses arranged in first and second directions;

a light-receiving unit including, for each of the plurality of micro-lenses, a plurality of corresponding light-receiving elements configured to receive respective light fluxes passing through different pupil regions of an imaging optical system and to output pupil-divided image signals;

a subject-image recognition unit configured to recognize a subject image represented by at least one of the pupil-divided image signals; and

a processor configured to:

perform phase-difference detection using the pupil-divided image signals to determine a defocus amount of the imaging optical system;

select, from among a plurality of defocus detection methods, a defocus detection method based on a result of the recognition of the subject image, the plurality of defocus detection methods differing in at least one of a signal-pairing direction, a detection region, a correlation-calculation condition, or a combination of the pupil-divided image signals; and

control focusing of the imaging optical system based on the defocus amount determined using the selected defocus detection method.

An imaging system comprising:

an imaging optical system configured to form an image of a subject on an image plane;

an image sensor including a plurality of pixels, at least a subset of the pixels constituting focus-detection pixels, each focus-detection pixel including a microlens and one or more photodetectors disposed to receive respective portions of a light flux passing through different pupil regions of the imaging optical system;

a signal-processing circuit configured to generate first and second focus-detection signals from outputs of the photodetectors, calculate a phase difference between the first and second focus-detection signals, and determine, based on the calculated phase difference, at least one of a defocus amount and a defocus direction;

a subject-recognition circuit configured to analyze image information obtained by the image sensor and recognize a characteristic of the subject, the characteristic including at least one of subject type, position, size, motion, contrast, luminance, color, texture, or occlusion state; and

a focus controller configured to adapt a focus-detection operation according to the recognized characteristic by selectively setting at least one of a focus-detection region, a group of focus-detection pixels, a correlation-calculation range, a signal-integration period, a weighting coefficient, a reliability threshold, or a lens-drive parameter, and to control movement of a focusing optical element based on the determined defocus amount and defocus direction.

The focus controller may further be configured to evaluate reliability of the phase-difference calculation, track the recognized subject across successive image frames, and dynamically modify the focus-detection operation such that focus is preferentially maintained on the recognized subject notwithstanding changes in subject position, motion, illumination, or image contrast.

1. An autofocus apparatus for a camera, comprising:  
an image-forming optical system;  
a photoelectric sensor configured to receive respective light fluxes passing through different pupil regions of the image-forming optical system and to generate corresponding image signals; and  
processing circuitry configured to:  
recognize a characteristic of an image represented by at least one of the image signals;  
select, according to the recognized characteristic, one of a plurality of defocus-detection methods that differ from one another in processing of the image signals;  
determine an amount of defocus of the image-forming optical system from the image signals using the selected defocus-detection method; and  
control focusing of the image-forming optical system based on the determined amount of defocus.

**1. An adaptive phase-detection autofocus sensor system comprising:**

a two-dimensional array of microlenses;

a two-dimensional array of photoelectric receiving elements arranged relative to the array of microlenses such that each of at least a plurality of the microlenses directs light from different portions of an exit pupil of an imaging lens onto respective receiving elements to generate phase-detection signals;

one or more processors; and

a memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to:

- obtain image data from at least a portion of the receiving elements;
- perform image recognition on the image data to determine a scene characteristic or an object characteristic;
- select, based on the determined scene characteristic or object characteristic, a defocus calculation technique from among a plurality of different defocus calculation techniques;
- calculate a defocus amount from the phase-detection signals using the selected defocus calculation technique; and
- generate, based on the calculated defocus amount, a focus-control signal for adjusting a focus state of the imaging lens,

wherein the plurality of different defocus calculation techniques differ in at least one of a correlation operation, a spatial region used for the correlation operation, a weighting applied to the phase-detection signals, a signal-combination operation, or a defocus conversion model.
